From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Prepare and enter
 hierarchical LPI through genpd

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

The constructed hierarchy has enough information to select parent domain
states and recover the exact FFH composite for the current CPU path. Define
the complete coordinated entry behavior before publishing it.

At the deepest non-WFI leaf state, suspend the virtual CPU consumer and let
genpd select leaf and shared ancestor states. Record each selected domain
state in its power-off callback, enter the deepest exact composite through
the architecture FFH hook, and resume the hierarchy afterward. Keep WFI and
shallower leaf states on the direct path.

Track logical consumer ownership separately from the paired direct genpd
suspend used on PREEMPT_RT. Use runtime PM for normal idle and an explicit
s2idle wrapper for suspend-to-idle accounting. Block hierarchy selection
while topology replacement or system sleep owns the domains, and allow
offline-only domains to be accounted without inventing a per-CPU FFH state.

If preparation or firmware entry fails, correct usage and rejection
counters for every selected state before clearing the per-attempt
selection. Preserve the correct s2idle context in that correction.

cpuidle records tick-broadcast requirements when the driver is registered.
A parent selected later can add context loss to the exact composite, so
collect architecture flags from every validated runtime path and advertise
their union on the coordinated leaf state before registration.

Record whether the root-most _LPI container has an _RDI object so the later
activation transaction can refuse unsupported resource dependencies. Define
the coordinated callbacks and prepared lifecycle state here, but keep them
unpublished and the genpd callbacks inert until activation changes firmware
mode.

